See, exactly. Look, everyone's saying it in chat: "Me, you, and Daigoro." That's right. What's that? Eh, what's that? I don't know it.

854
00:53:13,580 --> 00:53:16,280
キャッチフレーズみたいな...
It's like a catchphrase...

855
00:53:16,280 --> 00:53:20,580
なんじゃ、これ「アソビ★まわり隊！」で合う... 合うわけないじゃん！
What the... how could this match in Asobi Mawaritai?! There's no way it would match!

856
00:53:20,580 --> 00:53:24,080
これ、これもうキョーコがやってます。 キョーコやってます。
Kyoko is total PON here. I am doing it.

857
00:53:24,080 --> 00:53:30,080
ねぇ、しかも漢字で3文字だけど、ひらがなにすると「だいごろう」って6文字だよ！
Hey, plus it's 3 letters in Kanji, but if you write it in Hiragana, "da-i-go-ro-u" is 6 letters!

858
00:53:30,080 --> 00:53:33,080
いや、漢字とか言われてないから！ あ、文字か！
Hey, nobody said it had to be Kanji! Ah, it said letters!

859
00:53:33,080 --> 00:53:37,080
3文字って言ったら酒飲みは「大五郎」が出ちゃうのよ、どうしてもね！ 確か...
When you say 3 letters, alcohol lovers automatically think of "Daigoro", no matter what! Indeed...

860
00:53:37,080 --> 00:53:41,580
キョーコさん、リスナーから突っ込まれてますよ。 確かに！ 綴りのツッコミ...
Kyoko-san, the chat listeners are calling you out. True! Calling out your spelling...

861
00:53:41,580 --> 00:53:48,580
全然ッ... 全然じゃない... え、そんな... 今までも突っ込んでますけどね！
Not at all... wait, not quite... Eh, but... I've been pointing things out until now too!

862
00:53:48,580 --> 00:53:55,580
次行こうじゃあ！ あと5問だからね！ 「春の虫の定番といえば？」 あー、こんなの...
Let's move on then! 5 questions left! "What is the classic spring insect?" Ah, something like this...

863
00:53:55,580 --> 00:54:02,580
え、むず。 虫... 虫の... 春って... ま、春といえばこれかな。
Huh, that's hard. Insect... insect's... spring... Well, speaking of spring, maybe this.

864
00:54:02,580 --> 00:54:09,580
はい、やっぱこれだよね！ 晴れていたらね！ 何その声？ あれが飛んでいるイメージだよね。
Yes, it's gotta be this! When it's sunny! What's with that voice? You picture that flying around, right?

865
00:54:09,580 --> 00:54:14,580
これって虫でいいのか？ これ虫だよ！ 足6本か？
Is this actually considered an insect? It's an insect! Does it have 6 legs?

866
00:54:14,580 --> 00:54:20,080
6本足なら虫。 6本足は虫！ 6本足なん、こいつ？
If it has 6 legs, it's an insect. 6 legs means insect! Does this guy have 6 legs?

867
00:54:20,080 --> 00:54:28,080
一応、6本足は昆虫だから... そうね、広義の意味の... そう、虫ならクモとかも虫にカウントされたりはするけど。
Well, 6 legs make it an insect, so... Right, in a broad sense... Yeah, speaking of bugs, spiders get counted as bugs too.

868
00:54:28,080 --> 00:54:37,080
送ってみる。あ、まあ春っぽい、こいつを見かけたら春やなって思うやつってことじゃろ？ うん、そうそうそう。
I'll submit it. Ah, well, it feels like spring—when you see this guy, you feel like it's spring, right? Yeah, exactly, right.

869
00:54:37,080 --> 00:54:40,080
「ちょう」合ってるかも。行けるよ、これ！
"Chou" (butterfly) might be right. We can match on this!

870
00:54:40,080 --> 00:54:47,080
あーー！ たしかに！ なるほどね！ まあまあ、なるほどね。
Ahhh! Indeed! I see! Well well, I see.

871
00:54:47,080 --> 00:54:58,080
分かる分かる分かる。 ま、いるか。 確かに！ 確かにちょうちょも... なんかミツバチでさ、春なんかブンブン言ってるイメージがあるから蜂かなって思っちゃった。
I get it, I get it, I get it. Well, that exists too. Indeed! Indeed butterflies too... But like, honeybees make that buzzing sound in spring, so I thought of bees.

872
00:55:00,176 --> 00:55:03,088
書いたらさ、まずはチョウが飛んでるイメージ。
When you think of spring, first you imagine butterflies flying.

873
00:55:03,088 --> 00:55:04,588
ねー。
Right.

874
00:55:04,588 --> 00:55:08,588
６本足、６本足なの？チョウチョって。
Six legs? Butterflies have six legs?

875
00:55:08,588 --> 00:55:10,088
そうだよ。
That's right.

876
00:55:10,088 --> 00:55:13,588
あ、そうなんだ。ちょっと分からなかった。ごめん。
Oh, really? I didn't know that, sorry.

877
00:55:13,588 --> 00:55:16,588
これはお手上げ。
I really messed this one up.

878
00:55:16,588 --> 00:55:20,088
ちょっと難しいね。ハチも... ハチはまだ... うん、分かる分かる。
That was a bit tough. Bees... bees are still... yeah, I get it.

879
00:55:20,088 --> 00:55:22,588
うん、ミツバチは本当に春に飛ぶからね。
Yeah, honeybees really do fly around in spring.

880
00:55:22,588 --> 00:55:25,088
よかった、危なかった。
Whew, that was close!

881
00:55:25,088 --> 00:55:29,088
アウトなんですけど、アウトだけどまあセーフラインか、まだ。
I mean, it's out, but I guess it's still in the safe zone.

882
00:55:29,088 --> 00:55:31,088
許容範囲、全然。
Totally acceptable!

883
00:55:31,088 --> 00:55:33,588
ハチはいる。ハチは実際いるからね。
Bees are around. They're actually around in spring.

884
00:55:33,588 --> 00:55:36,588
うんうん、あるからあるから。
Yeah, yeah, it totally counts.

885
00:55:36,588 --> 00:55:38,088
行くのじゃ、次！
Let me go to the next one!

886
00:55:38,088 --> 00:55:40,588
孫悟空の決め技といえば？
Speaking of Goku's signature move?

887
00:55:40,588 --> 00:55:43,088
でもこんなの一致するんじゃない？
But everyone's definitely going to match on this!

888
00:55:43,088 --> 00:55:47,588
これ、違うの出したらだいぶ... だいぶなんじゃない？
If someone puts something different, it would be pretty... pretty bad, right?

889
00:55:47,588 --> 00:55:49,088
これびっくりするね、出さなかったら。
Yeah, I'd be shocked if someone didn't get it.

890
00:55:49,088 --> 00:55:52,588
これはね、分かる。
I know this one!

891
00:55:52,588 --> 00:55:56,588
え、待って。あ、あ、待って待って。合ってたかな、ちょっと待って。
Wait, hold on. Wait, wait, was it right? Wait a sec.

892
00:55:56,588 --> 00:55:59,588
え、待って、やばい、心配になってきた。
Wait, oh no, now I'm getting worried!

893
00:55:59,588 --> 00:56:03,588
一回深呼吸しよう。一回深呼吸しよう。でも送ってる送ってる。
Let me take a deep breath. Take a deep breath. But I already submitted it!

894
00:56:03,588 --> 00:56:06,588
送ったあとに言われてもね。
Saying that after submitting doesn't help!

895
00:56:06,588 --> 00:56:09,588
いや、違うの。合ってはいると思うの。
No, wait! I think I got the answer right...

896
00:56:09,588 --> 00:56:13,588
ただ、そのニュアンスを文字起こししたことがなくて...
It's just that I've never actually transcribed how it's spelled...

897
00:56:13,588 --> 00:56:15,588
文字起こし！？
Transcribed?!

898
00:56:15,588 --> 00:56:18,088
何の話をしてるの？
What are you talking about?

899
00:56:18,088 --> 00:56:21,088
言ったことはあるってことね？
You mean you've said it out loud before, right?

900
00:56:21,088 --> 00:56:24,088
言ったことはあるけど、そういう...
I've said it out loud, but...

901
00:56:24,088 --> 00:56:28,088
龍拳とか書いてきたら... 龍拳！？
What if someone wrote Ryuken... Ryuken?!

902
00:56:28,088 --> 00:56:31,588
どうする？全然違う作品の技書いてきたら？
What if someone wrote a move from a totally different anime?

903
00:56:31,588 --> 00:56:33,588
それはね、大丈夫。
Oh, that'll be fine.

904
00:56:33,588 --> 00:56:35,088
行くよ、つづり！
Let me click it, Tsuzuri!

905
00:56:35,088 --> 00:56:36,588
表示！
Reveal!

906
00:56:36,588 --> 00:56:38,588
え、合ってるんじゃない？
Wait, didn't we match?

907
00:56:38,588 --> 00:56:40,588
合ってる合ってる！
We matched, we matched!

908
00:56:40,588 --> 00:56:42,588
あれ？
Huh?

909
00:56:42,588 --> 00:56:47,088
かめかめになってる！
It says Kame-Kame!

910
00:56:47,088 --> 00:56:50,088
かめかめだ！
It's Kame-Kame!

911
00:56:50,088 --> 00:56:53,088
かめはめなんだ！
So it's Kamehame!

912
00:56:53,088 --> 00:56:56,088
かめはめなのよ！ちょっとムズい。
It IS Kamehame! That's a bit tricky.

913
00:56:56,088 --> 00:56:58,588
しかもなんでここだけカタカナなの？
And why is only this one in Katakana?

914
00:56:58,588 --> 00:57:03,088
確かに！かめかめはー！
That's true! "Kame-Kame-Ha!"

915
00:57:03,088 --> 00:57:07,588
見たことはちゃんとあったんだけどさ...
I've definitely seen it before, but...

916
00:57:07,588 --> 00:57:11,588
そっかー、かめはめめかー。
Oh, I see, it's Kamehame...

917
00:57:11,588 --> 00:57:14,088
かめはめなのよ！
It's Kamehame!

918
00:57:14,088 --> 00:57:18,088
これはしゃーない。正直、ミスる範囲だよ。
Can't be helped. To be honest, it's an understandable mistake.

919
00:57:18,088 --> 00:57:22,588
そっかー...
Ah, I see...

920
00:57:22,588 --> 00:57:25,588
気持ちは伝わってきたから大丈夫！次！
The intent got across, so it's fine! Next!

921
00:57:25,588 --> 00:57:28,088
ありはざ。鳥料理の定番といえば？
Thanks! Speaking of classic chicken dishes?

922
00:57:28,088 --> 00:57:31,088
これも、もうこれは分かるでしょ！
This one... surely everyone knows this!

923
00:57:31,088 --> 00:57:34,588
これはボーナス問題！
This is a bonus question!

924
00:57:34,588 --> 00:57:38,088
ドパろ、ドパろ！行くよ？
Let's match, let's match! Here I go!

925
00:57:38,088 --> 00:57:40,088
ドパりました！
Submitted!

926
00:57:40,088 --> 00:57:41,588
表示！
Reveal!

927
00:57:41,588 --> 00:57:45,088
やったー！からあげ！
Yay! Karaage!

928
00:57:45,088 --> 00:57:48,088
いやー、そうそう！
Oh yeah, exactly!

929
00:57:48,088 --> 00:57:52,088
言うことなしのからあげですよ！
Hands down, it's karaage!

930
00:57:52,088 --> 00:57:54,588
この調子で次行きますよ！
Keeping this momentum, let's go to the next one!

931
00:57:54,588 --> 00:57:56,588
よーし！
All right!

932
00:57:56,588 --> 00:57:58,588
今の状況を漢字一文字で表すと？
Describe the current situation in one Kanji character?

933
00:57:58,588 --> 00:58:02,088
え、ちょっと待って！
Wait a second!

934
00:58:02,088 --> 00:58:06,088
まずみんなが書ける漢字じゃなきゃいけなくて...
First, it has to be a Kanji everyone can write...

935
00:58:06,088 --> 00:58:09,588
確かに、確かに。常用漢字で...
True, true. A common kanji...

936
00:58:09,588 --> 00:58:13,588
今の状況... あ、分かった！あります！
Current situation... Ah, I got it! I have one!

937
00:58:13,588 --> 00:58:17,088
これぐらい？すごく良いのある！
About this? I have a really good one!

938
00:58:17,088 --> 00:58:20,088
これかな？これだよな。
This one? Must be this one.

939
00:58:20,088 --> 00:58:24,088
うん、これ。何？ヒント頂戴、わし分かってないから。
Yeah, this. What? Give me a hint, I don't get it.

940
00:58:24,088 --> 00:58:28,088
これがいっぱい、いっぱいっぱい。
We're full of this, super full.

941
00:58:28,088 --> 00:58:31,088
私もしっかりそれ。うん、いっぱい。
I'm full of that too. Yeah, super full.

942
00:58:31,088 --> 00:58:35,088
本当は「たん」で行きたいところだけど... あ、分かった！
Ideally I'd want to go with "tan", but... Ah, I get it!

943
00:58:35,088 --> 00:58:39,588
って言ったら違う漢字になるよね。つづりが書ける漢字ってことは...
If you say that, it becomes a different kanji. But if it's a kanji Tsuzuri can write...

944
00:58:39,588 --> 00:58:43,088
そう。「たん」って何？
Right. What's "tan"?

945
00:58:43,088 --> 00:58:47,088
考えなくていいや、難しくなっちゃうかも。
Don't think about it, it might get confusing.

946
00:58:47,088 --> 00:58:51,088
別の漢字がくっつくから、うちは。
Because another kanji attaches to it on my end.

947
00:58:51,088 --> 00:58:55,088
ごめん、間違えたかも！
Sorry, I might have messed up!

948
00:58:55,088 --> 00:58:59,088
え、何？言ったような...
What? Like what was said...

949
00:58:59,088 --> 00:59:03,588
つづりちゃんのが分からない。表示！
I don't know what Tsuzuri wrote. Reveal!

950
00:59:03,588 --> 00:59:08,588
そっちね！そっちね！
That one! You meant that one!

951
00:59:08,588 --> 00:59:14,088
それつづりだけないよ！4人を巻き込まないでいただいて...
Only Tsuzuri wrote that! Please don't drag the four of us into it...

952
00:59:14,088 --> 00:59:18,588
難しくはないかな、うちらはね。
It wasn't hard for us.

953
00:59:18,588 --> 00:59:23,588
つづりと言えばって言ってたから、今のつづりの状況はこれかなって...
You said "Speaking of Tsuzuri", so I thought Tsuzuri's current situation is this...

954
00:59:23,588 --> 00:59:28,088
恥の多い生涯を... 太宰が来た！
"A life filled with shame..." Dazai has arrived!

955
00:59:28,088 --> 00:59:31,588
いやー、やったー。
Man, yay!

956
00:59:31,588 --> 00:59:35,088
でも確かに分かるわ、「草」も分かるし「笑」も分かるわ。
But I do get it, "grass" (lol) makes sense and "smile/laugh" makes sense.

957
00:59:35,088 --> 00:59:39,088
あれでしょ？「たん」って短芝の話でしょ？
Right? By "tan" you meant short grass, right?

958
00:59:39,088 --> 00:59:41,088
そう、短芝の話。
Yeah, short grass.

959
00:59:41,088 --> 00:59:44,088
じゃあ残念でしたと。
So that was unfortunate.

960
00:59:44,088 --> 00:59:49,088
上3人にはちょっと合っていたが、自分1人にしか合ってはらへん。
The top 3 kind of matched, but you only matched with yourself.

961
00:59:49,088 --> 00:59:53,088
ちょっとそれ多いな！自分語りが多いんだ。
You do that a lot! Self-referential answers happen too often.

962
00:59:53,088 --> 01:00:00,088
いや、だって今「つづり、つづりかな」って言ってたから...
No, because just now someone said "Tsuzuri, maybe Tsuzuri"...

963
01:00:00,096 --> 01:00:02,256
なんかなって思ってつづりの心境を...
I was like "what is this...", describing Tsuzuri's mental state...

964
01:00:02,596 --> 01:00:06,096
つづりにこれね、あの、笑い笑い草草って感じ...
Tsuzuri wrote this, like "lol lol grass grass"...

965
01:00:06,396 --> 01:00:10,096
確かに！マジ草！この状況マジ草！
Indeed! Really grass! This situation is really grass!

966
01:00:10,096 --> 01:00:13,596
並んでるよ！つづりワロタ！ワロタ！
It's lined up! Tsuzuri warota! Warota!

967
01:00:13,596 --> 01:00:16,596
マジワロタ！
Seriously warota!

968
01:00:17,096 --> 01:00:19,096
次行くぞしゃ！はい！
Let's move on to the next one! Alright!

969
01:00:19,696 --> 01:00:23,096
はい！日本を代表する芸術家といえば？
Yes! Speaking of an artist representing Japan?

970
01:00:23,196 --> 01:00:24,696
むっず！これむっず！
Hard! This is so hard!

971
01:00:24,896 --> 01:00:27,596
いや、これね、浮かぶんだけど...
No, I mean, someone comes to mind, but...

972
01:00:27,596 --> 01:00:31,096
わしメロウとかじゃダメ？メラメラとかじゃダメ？
Can't I say Melopolice or something? Can't I say Mera-mera or something?

973
01:00:31,096 --> 01:00:34,596
メラメラで行きますか？あ！逆に分かんないそれ！
Shall we go with Mera-mera? Ah! On the contrary, I don't get that!

974
01:00:34,596 --> 01:00:39,096
なんか...なんじゃろ。ほら昔というか、わしが生まれて...
Something... what was it. See, old times or like, since I was born...

975
01:00:39,096 --> 01:00:46,596
すでにあの配信とかでもきっと...ちらっと関連するものに触れたことがあるような...
Already, even in streams, we've probably touched upon something related to it...

976
01:00:47,096 --> 01:00:51,596
触れましたね！うちのね、近くで触れましたね、あれ！
We touched upon it! Near my place, we touched upon that!

977
01:00:51,596 --> 01:00:54,096
え、どの...どれの、どのやつにすればいいんだろう？その人...
Wait, which... which of his names should I use? That person...

978
01:00:54,096 --> 01:00:57,096
名義は？正しい名義で...
As for the name? Use his official name...

979
01:00:57,096 --> 01:01:00,096
あ、あ、あ、これが答え！代表する...
Ah ah ah, this is the answer! Representing...

980
01:01:01,596 --> 01:01:06,596
やばい、ごめん。もっとヒントくれ！もっとヒントくれ！頼む！
Oh no, sorry. Give me more hints! Give me more hints, please!

981
01:01:06,596 --> 01:01:13,096
えっと...わしはいつ生まれたのじゃろうか...
Well... when was I born, I wonder...

982
01:01:13,096 --> 01:01:16,596
え？江戸でしょう？え？江戸でしょう？
Eh? Edo, right? Eh? Edo, right?

983
01:01:16,596 --> 01:01:21,596
代表する...芸術...やばい、つづりが分からんか？
Representing... art... oh no, does Tsuzuri not know?

984
01:01:21,596 --> 01:01:24,096
あ！言っちゃった、もう！
Ah! You said it already!

985
01:01:24,096 --> 01:01:27,596
いや、あの、昔のさ...そうそうそう。
No, like, from the past... yeah yeah yeah.

986
01:01:27,596 --> 01:01:31,096
ほら...浮世絵まで言っちゃいます？浮世絵の...
Look... should I go as far as saying ukiyo-e? Ukiyo-e...

987
01:01:31,096 --> 01:01:37,096
有名な！昔の超有名な！水をね、こう...バシャーンとね...
Famous! Super famous from old times! Water, like this... splash...

988
01:01:39,096 --> 01:01:44,596
水...あ！分かった！分かった！分かった！これだ！これだ！
Water... Ah! I got it! I got it! I got it! This is it! This is it!

989
01:01:52,096 --> 01:01:58,096
「かつしか」で出てくる人、初めて見た！大体「北斎」だろう！
I've never seen anyone answer with just "Katsushika"! Usually people say "Hokusai"!

990
01:01:58,096 --> 01:02:03,096
すげえな！逆に！出るならいいじゃん！「かつしか」出た！
Amazing! On the contrary! If it comes out, it's fine! "Katsushika" came out!

991
01:02:03,096 --> 01:02:07,096
どちらかというと「北斎」だけで行くよね！
If anything, people would just go with "Hokusai"!

992
01:02:07,096 --> 01:02:10,096
あぶねー、よかったー...
That was close, thank goodness...

993
01:02:10,096 --> 01:02:15,096
でも...すごい！えらい！よくがんばったつづり！素晴らしいのじゃ！
But... incredible! Great job! You did well, Tsuzuri! Wonderful!

994
01:02:15,096 --> 01:02:19,096
いや、よく出たよ！よく出た！
No, you did really well to come up with it! Well done!

995
01:02:19,096 --> 01:02:22,096
「江戸」って言ってくれてよかった...よかった、よかった...
I'm so glad you said "Edo"... Thank goodness...

996
01:02:22,096 --> 01:02:25,096
やっぱね、メタで合わせるのがね...
After all, matching meta-wise is...

997
01:02:25,096 --> 01:02:30,096
ありがとう、助かった...ほんと太郎とか書こうとしてたからさ...
Thank you, that saved me... I was literally about to write Taro...

998
01:02:30,096 --> 01:02:34,096
ね！時代で考えるとむずいよな。
Right! Thinking about the era makes it hard.

999
01:02:34,096 --> 01:02:40,096
ちなみにあのそぴあが書いてるあの北斎が、あの老年期、晩年に...
By the way, the Hokusai that Sopia wrote is the old age, late years...

1000
01:02:40,096 --> 01:02:44,096
一番最後の一番最後のやつよね？一番最後また戻ったんだ。
It's the very very last one, right? He returned to it at the very end.

1001
01:02:44,096 --> 01:02:48,096
北斎、「画狂老人卍」って名乗ってたらしいっていう。
Apparently Hokusai called himself "Gakyo Rojin Manji".

1002
01:02:48,096 --> 01:02:51,096
ペンネームね！かっこいい！そうなのか！
Pen name, right! So cool! Is that so?!

1003
01:02:51,096 --> 01:02:55,096
そうそう。やっぱあの...
Yeah yeah. After all...

1004
01:02:55,096 --> 01:02:58,096
なんかすごい現代に通じるセンスしてるよね！
He had a sense that really connects with modern times!

1005
01:02:58,096 --> 01:03:01,096
結構いろんな名義があるんだよね。
He had quite a few different pseudonyms.

1006
01:03:01,096 --> 01:03:04,096
別名義結構さ、Twitterとかにいそうな名前って言ってね。
Pseudonyms that sound like Twitter usernames, you know.

1007
01:03:04,096 --> 01:03:07,096
ホント面白いんだよね！
It's really interesting!

1008
01:03:10,096 --> 01:03:15,096
なんて名前かは言わんけど、今のツイッターにいそうな名前の時代もあった。
I won't say what name it was, but there was an era where his name sounded like a modern Twitter user.

1009
01:03:15,096 --> 01:03:18,096
そうそうそう！通じるものがある、マジで！
Yes yes yes! There's definitely a shared vibe, seriously!

1010
01:03:18,096 --> 01:03:20,096
じゃあ、次行きますか。
Well then, shall we go to the next one?

1011
01:03:20,096 --> 01:03:26,096
よいしょ！えーっと、ピンクの服を着ている芸能人といえば？
Alright! Um, speaking of a celebrity who wears pink clothes?

1012
01:03:26,096 --> 01:03:28,096
あ、なるほどね！
Ah, I see!

1013
01:03:28,596 --> 01:03:31,596
え、今ね、私2人出てる。横並びで。
Wait, right now 2 people came to my mind. Side by side.

1014
01:03:31,596 --> 01:03:37,096
え、待って。強豪いた？いや分かんない。どのあれかな？
Wait. Is there a strong competitor? I don't know. Which one would it be?

1015
01:03:37,096 --> 01:03:41,096
芸能人っていうの広いからな。2人ともピンクで私出てる、今。
Celebrity is a broad category, though. Both of them in pink came to my mind now.

1016
01:03:41,096 --> 01:03:43,096
2人ともピンク？
Both of them in pink?

1017
01:03:43,096 --> 01:03:51,096
ピンク...そぴあがパッと思い浮かんだのあの人だけど、みんなが知ってるのかな？
Pink... the person Sopia instantly thought of is that person, but does everyone know them?

1018
01:03:51,096 --> 01:03:54,096
じゃあ多分同じのじゃない？
Then it's probably the same one, right?

1019
01:03:54,096 --> 01:03:57,096
え、じゃあ多分さ、そぴあさ、「つーちゃん」って感じの人？「つーちゃん」！
Wait, so probably Sopia, the person you're thinking of is like "Tsu-chan"? "Tsu-chan"!

1020
01:03:57,096 --> 01:04:00,096
あ！分かった！分かった！多分この人だ！
Ah! I got it! I got it! Probably this person!

1021
01:04:00,096 --> 01:04:04,096
ん？つーちゃん？お名前が分かんないかも...
Hmm? Tsu-chan? I might not know the name...

1022
01:04:04,096 --> 01:04:06,096
あ、じゃあやめとこっか！
Ah, then let's avoid it!

1023
01:04:06,096 --> 01:04:09,096
え、でも、「つーちゃん」で行けるのよね？
Wait, but we can go with "Tsu-chan", right?

1024
01:04:09,096 --> 01:04:12,096
「つーちゃん」「つーちゃん」って感じでしょう？
It feels like "Tsu-chan", "Tsu-chan", right?

1025
01:04:12,096 --> 01:04:16,096
ちょっと呼び捨てになっちゃうけどいいかな？この人だ、分かった！
It's a bit without honorifics, but is it okay? It's this person, got it!

1026
01:04:16,096 --> 01:04:20,096
え？ピンクの服着てる人でしょ？じゃあ「つーちゃん」でしょう？
Eh? The person wearing pink, right? Then it's "Tsu-chan", right?

1027
01:04:20,096 --> 01:04:24,096
え？これかこっちか...あー分かった分かった！
Wait? This one or that one... Ah, I got it, I got it!

1028
01:04:24,096 --> 01:04:31,096
えっとね、私が想像してるのは違うけど、多分つーちゃんこっちを想像してるんだろうなで行くわ。
Um, what I'm imagining is different, but I'll go with what Tsu-chan is probably imagining.

1029
01:04:31,096 --> 01:04:33,096
にょけい？
Are you okay?

1030
01:04:33,096 --> 01:04:35,096
うん、大丈夫。
Yeah, I'm okay.

1031
01:04:35,096 --> 01:04:37,096
うん、多分この人！
Yeah, probably this person!

1032
01:04:37,096 --> 01:04:40,096
オッケー！いってみるのじゃ！はい！
Okay! Let me reveal! Yes!

1033
01:04:40,096 --> 01:04:42,096
いくのじゃ！表示！
Here we go! Display!

1034
01:04:42,096 --> 01:04:46,096
えーー！？
Ehh?!

1035
01:04:46,096 --> 01:04:51,096
なんかさ、ピンクの服着ててさ、パンチパーマの方いらっしゃらなかったっけ？
Wait, wearing pink clothes, and wasn't there a person with a punch perm?

1036
01:04:51,096 --> 01:04:54,096
いるけど、なんで「つーちゃん」からそこ行ったのかなっていうのが今...
There is, but why did you jump there from "Tsu-chan"? That's what I'm wondering...

1037
01:04:54,096 --> 01:04:58,096
「つーちゃんペーさん」みたいな感じで...
Like "Tsu-chan, Pe-san" kind of feel...

1038
01:04:58,096 --> 01:05:00,196
ペーパーさんかな？
Pā-Pē-san maybe?

1039
01:05:01,404 --> 01:05:02,654
あ、林家ペーさんね？
Ah, Hayashiya Pe-san, right?

1040
01:05:02,654 --> 01:05:05,004
あ、ペーパーだからつづり言ったってこと？
Ah, so Tsuzuri said Pe because of "paper"?

1041
01:05:05,004 --> 01:05:07,004
ペーさんって呼ばれてなかった？ 紙だからってこと？ えー！？
Wasn't he called Pe-san? Because it's paper? What?!

1042
01:05:07,004 --> 01:05:08,604
コミだからってこと？ えー？
Wait, because of comic? What?

1043
01:05:08,604 --> 01:05:10,104
そういうこと？ え、どういうこと？
Is that why? Wait, what do you mean?

1044
01:05:10,104 --> 01:05:11,504
わかってない。
I don't get it.

1045
01:05:14,404 --> 01:05:17,604
え、なんか、どちらかというとキョーコはつづりに合わせようとして...
Like, if anything, Kyoko tried to match Tsuzuri...

1046
01:05:17,604 --> 01:05:23,004
つづりの世界観に合わせようとして、多分分かりやすいのにしてくれたんだよね？
Tried to match Tsuzuri's worldview, and probably made it easy to understand, right?

1047
01:05:23,004 --> 01:05:26,204
え、そう、それでチャンピオンズにしようと思って...
Yeah, so I thought of going with Champions...

1048
01:05:26,204 --> 01:05:27,004
はい。
Yes.

1049
01:05:27,004 --> 01:05:29,904
「ダイちゃん」だから「ツゥちゃん」みたいな感じだよ、って言ったら...
When I said, "Since it's Dai-chan, it's like Tsuu-chan"...

1050
01:05:29,904 --> 01:05:35,404
多分通じてなさそうだったから、「あ、これトゥースを連想してるのかな」って思ってオードリー春日にしたって感じ。
She didn't seem to get it, so I thought, "Ah, maybe she's associating it with Tooth," and went with Audrey Kasuga.

1051
01:05:35,404 --> 01:05:36,604
あ、逆に！
Ah, the opposite!

1052
01:05:36,604 --> 01:05:40,004
なんか「トゥース」って感じじゃなかったから、「あ、じゃあ春日さんじゃない」って言って...
It didn't feel like "Tooth", so I said, "Ah, then it's not Kasuga-san"...

1053
01:05:40,004 --> 01:05:44,304
あの、お二方いらっしゃるじゃん。双子さん...
You know, there's that pair. The twins...

1054
01:05:44,304 --> 01:05:47,404
双子さんの芸能人さん。歌上手い...
The twin celebrities who sing well...

1055
01:05:47,404 --> 01:05:49,104
おすぎとピー... あ、そっちじゃないか！
Osugi and Pi... Ah, wait, not them!

1056
01:05:52,604 --> 01:05:55,304
そっち違うってなって...
Then I realized it wasn't them...

1057
01:05:55,304 --> 01:06:01,104
あ、真っピンクの人確かに洋服着た姉さん出た！と思って思い浮かんだのがペーさんだったの。
I remembered that sister who wears bright pink clothes! And the one that popped into my head was Pe-san!

1058
01:06:01,104 --> 01:06:04,604
呼び捨てかよ！
You omitted the honorific!

1059
01:06:04,604 --> 01:06:07,904
やばい、考えすぎて逆にダメなの、めちゃ難しい！
Oh no, overthinking makes it worse, it's super hard!

1060
01:06:07,904 --> 01:06:09,604
いや、難しい！
Yeah, it's hard!

1061
01:06:09,604 --> 01:06:12,104
姉妹のことか... あの二人ちなみに姉妹ですらしからね。
You meant the sisters... By the way, those two aren't even sisters.

1062
01:06:12,104 --> 01:06:13,604
あ、そうなの！？ 姉妹だと思ってた。
Ah, really?! I thought they were sisters.

1063
01:06:13,604 --> 01:06:15,104
姉妹ですらない。
They aren't even sisters.

1064
01:06:15,104 --> 01:06:16,904
え、そうなの！？
Eh, really?!

1065
01:06:16,904 --> 01:06:18,004
うん。
Yeah.

1066
01:06:18,004 --> 01:06:19,604
混ざってたっけ？
Did I get them mixed up?

1067
01:06:19,604 --> 01:06:21,104
ええー！
Ehh?!

1068
01:06:21,104 --> 01:06:22,604
そうだったんだ。
Is that so.

1069
01:06:22,604 --> 01:06:25,104
超面白かったね。次行ってみよう！
That was super funny. Let's move to the next one!

1070
01:06:25,104 --> 01:06:28,204
[Title: パプリカって何色？] パプリカって何色？
[Title: What color is paprika?] What color is paprika?

1071
01:06:28,204 --> 01:06:30,104
え、これ二択じゃないかい！
Wait, isn't this a two-choice question?!

1072
01:06:30,104 --> 01:06:32,504
二択だが...
It's two choices, but...

1073
01:06:32,504 --> 01:06:35,104
50%... いや、これはもう何のノーヒントで...
50%... No, with zero hints...

1074
01:06:35,104 --> 01:06:39,004
これを一発で当てさせていただきます！
I'll get this right on the first try!

1075
01:06:39,004 --> 01:06:42,604
これ当てたいよ、二択だから！
I want to get this right since it's two choices!

1076
01:06:42,604 --> 01:06:45,104
気持ちよく当てたいな。
I want a satisfying match.

1077
01:06:45,104 --> 01:06:46,704
行くのじゃ！ 表示！
Here we go! Display!

1078
01:06:46,704 --> 01:06:52,104
[Text: 赤 / 赤色 / 赤 / 赤] やったーーー！！
[Text: Red / Red color / Red / Red] Yayyyy!!

1079
01:06:52,104 --> 01:06:56,604
これはデカい！ 2択を当てて繋げられました！
This is huge! We got the two-choice right and kept the streak going!

1080
01:06:56,604 --> 01:06:58,304
ありがとうござんす！
Thank you very much!

1081
01:06:58,304 --> 01:07:04,104
のじゃ！ 黄色か悩むけどね。素晴らしい！ これが以心伝心の力っちゅうことですのじゃ。
Indeed! Though I hesitated with yellow. Wonderful! This is the power of telepathy.

1082
01:07:04,104 --> 01:07:07,104
[Title: 空を飛ぶ以外で、魔法使いの定番魔法といえば？] 空を飛ぶ以外で、魔法使いの定番魔法といえば？
[Title: Besides flying in the sky, what is a classic magic spell for a wizard?] Besides flying in the sky, what is a classic magic spell for a wizard?

1083
01:07:07,104 --> 01:07:10,104
来たー！ これいけるよ、主ら！
It's here! We can do this, guys!

1084
01:07:10,104 --> 01:07:13,904
あと2問だよ！ えっ、いけんじゃん！ 終わりが見えてきたよ。
Just 2 questions left! Wait, we can do this! The end is in sight.

1085
01:07:13,904 --> 01:07:18,104
空を飛ぶ以外で、魔法使いの定番魔法といえば...
Besides flying in the sky, what is a classic magic spell for a wizard...

1086
01:07:18,104 --> 01:07:23,604
一瞬シーンってなったくらい、みんな頭フル回転してんじゃない？
Everyone's brains are spinning so fast it went dead silent for a second!

1087
01:07:23,604 --> 01:07:27,104
でもちょっと、うちらメタにもなってるけど...
But wait, it's kinda related to our meta too...

1088
01:07:27,104 --> 01:07:30,604
メラ...？ 魔法...魔法か？
Mera...? Magic... is it magic?

1089
01:07:30,604 --> 01:07:35,104
あ、うちらメタね！ 今2個で迷ってたけど、オッケー！
Ah, our meta, right! I was torn between 2, but okay!

1090
01:07:35,104 --> 01:07:37,104
これしかないじゃん、じゃあ！
Then it can only be this!

1091
01:07:37,104 --> 01:07:40,104
ウィンガーディアム・レヴィオーサ...
Wingardium Leviosa...

1092
01:07:40,104 --> 01:07:44,104
え、何それ！？ 違う違う！
Eh, what's that?! No no no!

1093
01:07:44,104 --> 01:07:48,104
うちらと言えばでいいでしょ？
It's okay to go with what represents us, right?

1094
01:07:48,104 --> 01:07:51,104
うちらと言えば！
What represents us!

1095
01:07:51,104 --> 01:07:55,604
一番に思いついたのこれしかなかった。
This was the only thing I thought of first.

1096
01:07:55,604 --> 01:08:00,104
え、行ってみる？ 分かんないけど行ってみるか。
Eh, shall we submit? I don't know, but let's try.

1097
01:08:00,104 --> 01:08:04,104
行くのじゃ！ よいしょ！
Here we go! Yoisho!

1098
01:08:04,104 --> 01:08:07,604
[Text: メラ / ワープ / 火 / めら] あーーー！！
[Text: Mera / Warp / Fire / Mera] Ahhhh!!

1099
01:08:07,604 --> 01:08:10,604
惜しい！
So close!

1100
01:08:10,604 --> 01:08:15,104
言ったじゃん！ うちらと言えばでよー！
I told you! What represents us!

1101
01:08:15,104 --> 01:08:18,104
あ、ワープ誰か... 洗濯機だ！
Ah, warp is someone... It's the washing machine!

1102
01:08:18,104 --> 01:08:22,104
洗濯機だ！
It's the washing machine!

1103
01:08:22,104 --> 01:08:27,604
洗濯機あれじゃん、うちらの場所色々移動できる... ワープができるからあそこ！
The washing machine can move us to various places... Because it can warp there!

1104
01:08:27,604 --> 01:08:31,104
なるほどね！
I see!

1105
01:08:31,104 --> 01:08:35,104
難しかったな... そこパッと思い出すのは確かに魔法か。
That was hard... Instantly recalling that is indeed magic.

1106
01:08:35,104 --> 01:08:40,104
わしの本能になれすぎてね。
I'm too accustomed to my own instinct.

1107
01:08:40,104 --> 01:08:44,104
めっちゃはてな自分で書いてあるじゃん！
You wrote so many question marks yourself!

1108
01:08:44,104 --> 01:08:51,104
おこがましいかなと思って... うちらって言ったのにわし1人ってちょっと違うかなと思って悩んじゃった。
I thought it might be presumptuous... I thought if you said 'us', having just me might be off, so I hesitated.

1109
01:08:51,104 --> 01:08:55,104
メラのことだったよ！ めらって書いてるよ。
It was about Mera! I wrote Mera.

1110
01:08:55,104 --> 01:08:57,104
右下のは何？
What's the bottom right one?

1111
01:08:57,104 --> 01:09:01,104
え、なんか火出してるやつ... 魔法唱えて。
Eh, someone casting fire magic...

1112
01:09:01,104 --> 01:09:04,104
ぽんぽんぽんって飛んでいかなかったっけ？ キメラって。
Didn't Chimera fly off pom pom pom?

1113
01:09:04,104 --> 01:09:06,104
一発だけ。
Just one hit.

1114
01:09:06,104 --> 01:09:09,104
一発だけ？ 人？ 人と火って感じ？
Just one hit? A person? Person and fire?

1115
01:09:09,104 --> 01:09:14,104
大体一発だね、メラは。敵単体に小ダメージだから。
Usually one hit for Mera. Small damage to single enemy.

1116
01:09:14,104 --> 01:09:17,104
今のメラゾーマではないのじゃ。次に行くのじゃ！
What I used just now wasn't Merazoma. Let's move to the next!

1117
01:09:17,104 --> 01:09:20,104
メラじゃ！
It's Mera!

1118
01:09:20,104 --> 01:09:24,104
[Title: 誕生日以外で、プレゼントをもらう定番イベントといえば？] 誕生日以外で、プレゼントをもらう定番イベントといえば？
[Title: Besides birthdays, what is a classic event to receive presents?] Besides birthdays, what is a classic event to receive presents?

1119
01:09:24,104 --> 01:09:27,104
これ来たんじゃないかい！ これ行っとこう！ これ以外ないよね！
Didn't this just come! Let's go with this! There's nothing besides this!

1120
01:09:27,104 --> 01:09:32,104
わし欲しいけどな。プレゼント欲しいけどな、何くれるんだろ。
I want presents though. I want presents, what will they give?

1121
01:09:32,104 --> 01:09:35,104
みんなで交換しようか！
Shall we exchange among ourselves!

1122
01:09:35,104 --> 01:09:38,104
つづり言ってお届けするやつ？
The one where Tsuzuri delivers?

1123
01:09:38,104 --> 01:09:42,604
つづり届けてほしいね！ あ、間違えた、それじゃない！
We want Tsuzuri to deliver! Ah wait, not that!

1124
01:09:42,604 --> 01:09:48,104
つづりは、多分外部委託するんじゃないか。
Tsuzuri would probably outsource it.

1125
01:09:48,104 --> 01:09:51,104
業務形態の話をちょっと... そっちじゃないね！
Talking about business structure... not that!

1126
01:09:51,104 --> 01:09:56,604
でも多分これだよね、これな気がする！
But it's probably this, feels like this!

1127
01:09:56,604 --> 01:09:59,104
行くのじゃ！ 表示！
Here we go! Display!

1128
01:09:59,104 --> 01:10:00,104
[Text: クリスマス / クリスマス / クリスマス / クリスマス] やったーーー！！
[Text: Christmas / Christmas / Christmas / Christmas] Yayyyy!!

1129
01:10:00,112 --> 01:10:01,412
「あー！」
"Aah!"

1130
01:10:01,412 --> 01:10:03,112
「やったー！」
"We did it!"

1131
01:10:03,112 --> 01:10:04,912
「よかったー！」
"Thank goodness!"

1132
01:10:04,912 --> 01:10:07,612
「よかったー！」
"What a relief!"

1133
01:10:07,612 --> 01:10:10,612
「つづりちゃんのおじいちゃんにね、頼めばいいからね、こっちはね」
"We can just ask Tsuzuri-chan's grandpa for this one, right?"

1134
01:10:10,612 --> 01:10:11,912
「うん」
"Yeah."

1135
01:10:11,912 --> 01:10:13,612
「つづりちゃん自身じゃない」「よかったよかった」
"It's not Tsuzuri-chan herself." / "Thank goodness."

1136
01:10:13,612 --> 01:10:15,612
「つづりちゃんお正月には働くもんね、いっぱいね」
"Tsuzuri-chan will be working a lot during the New Year's holidays, after all."

1137
01:10:15,612 --> 01:10:17,112
「いっぱい働きます」
"I'll work super hard."

1138
01:10:17,112 --> 01:10:18,112
「そうそう」
"Right, right."

1139
01:10:18,112 --> 01:10:20,112
「配りにいきます、お正月」
"I'll go deliver mail during New Year's."

1140
01:10:20,112 --> 01:10:21,612
「うわ、あと1問だよ！」
"Whoa, only 1 question left!"

1141
01:10:21,612 --> 01:10:22,912
「つらいんだ、大変なんだね」
"It must be tough and hard work."

1142
01:10:22,912 --> 01:10:24,612
「はい、頑張ります」
"Yes, I'll do my best."

1143
01:10:24,612 --> 01:10:25,912
「かわいい！」
"So cute!"

1144
01:10:25,912 --> 01:10:28,112
「それでは、次の問題なのじゃ」
"Well then, on to the next question!"

1145
01:10:28,112 --> 01:10:29,612
「あと1問だよ！」
"Only 1 question left!"

1146
01:10:29,612 --> 01:10:31,112
「うー！」「これ！」
"Ooh!" / "This one!"

1147
01:10:31,112 --> 01:10:34,112
「もう2択だ！」「いけるんじゃない？」
"It's down to two options!" / "Can't we get this?"

1148
01:10:34,112 --> 01:10:36,912
[Title: 高身長が最も有利なスポーツといえば？]
[Title: Speaking of a sport where being tall is most advantageous?]

1149
01:10:36,912 --> 01:10:39,612
「これ2択だから」「これ2択だわ」
"Since it's between two choices..." / "This really is a choice between two."

1150
01:10:39,612 --> 01:10:41,612
「ちょっと、2択はヒントなしで決めたいな」
"Hold on, since it's a two-way choice, I want us to decide without hints."

1151
01:10:41,612 --> 01:10:44,912
「あ、でも…いや、これあー…」「身長…」
"Ah, but... no, is this...?" / "Height..."

1152
01:10:45,112 --> 01:10:48,112
「うわ、むずいな！どっちかなー？」
"Whoa, that's tough! Which one could it be?"

1153
01:10:48,112 --> 01:10:50,312
「いや、でもこっちじゃないかな」「流れ的にね」
"Nah, but wouldn't it be this one?" / "Given the flow of things."

1154
01:10:50,312 --> 01:10:52,312
「流れ的にね」
"Given the flow."

1155
01:10:52,312 --> 01:10:54,112
「わかる」「わかるわかるわかる」
"I get it." / "I know, I know, I know."

1156
01:10:54,112 --> 01:10:55,612
「じゃあこっちだ」「いってみよう」
"Then it's this one." / "Let me go with this."

1157
01:10:55,612 --> 01:10:57,912
「じゃあこれだ！」「いこう、じゃあ！」「よいしょ！」
"Then it's this!" / "Let me submit, then!" / "Here goes!"

1158
01:10:58,112 --> 01:10:59,312
「えっ！？」
"Huh?!"

1159
01:10:59,312 --> 01:11:03,612
「やったー！」「すごーい！」「すごい！」
"Yay!" / "Awesome!" / "Amazing!"

1160
01:11:03,612 --> 01:11:05,612
「いけたじゃん、うち等！」「すごーい！」
"We pulled it off!" / "Awesome!"

1161
01:11:05,612 --> 01:11:07,112
「すごいすごいすごい！」
"Amazing, amazing, amazing!"

1162
01:11:07,112 --> 01:11:09,612
「全問正解なのじゃ！」
"We got all of them right!"

1163
01:11:09,612 --> 01:11:11,312
「全問正解だ！」「やったー！」
"All correct!" / "Yay!"

1164
01:11:11,312 --> 01:11:13,312
「すごすぎる！」「10問合ってるよ、私達！」
"Too amazing!" / "We got 10 questions right!"

1165
01:11:13,312 --> 01:11:14,612
「よかったー」
"Thank goodness..."

1166
01:11:14,612 --> 01:11:16,112
「すごすぎる！」「すごい！」
"Too amazing!" / "Awesome!"

1167
01:11:16,112 --> 01:11:18,612
「すごくない？だって前回さ、30分で…」
"Isn't this amazing? Because last time, in 30 minutes..."

1168
01:11:18,612 --> 01:11:21,112
「3問？」「3問しか行かなかった」
"3 questions?" / "We only cleared 3 questions!"

1169
01:11:21,112 --> 01:11:22,612
「で、今回は？」
"And this time?"

1170
01:11:22,612 --> 01:11:24,112
「あ、でも1時間で」
"Ah, but in 1 hour..."

1171
01:11:24,112 --> 01:11:26,312
「ちょっと早くなった！」「ちょっと早くなった！」
"It got a little bit faster!" / "It got a little bit faster!"

1172
01:11:26,312 --> 01:11:28,112
「だいぶすごいよ！」「すごいじゃない！」
"That's pretty awesome!" / "Isn't that awesome?"

1173
01:11:28,112 --> 01:11:30,112
「すごーい！」「やったー！」
"Awesome!" / "Yay!"

1174
01:11:30,112 --> 01:11:32,112
「分かり合えてるんじゃない？」
"Aren't we understanding each other better?"

1175
01:11:32,112 --> 01:11:34,112
「あの時よりもさらに絆深まってるってことだよ、これは！」
"This means our bond has deepened even more since that time!"

1176
01:11:34,112 --> 01:11:36,112
「うん！」「しかもなんか…」
"Yeah!" / "And plus..."

1177
01:11:36,112 --> 01:11:39,612
「だんだんさ、加速度的に正解増えてったよね！」
"Bit by bit, our correct answers increased exponentially, right?"

1178
01:11:39,612 --> 01:11:41,112
「ねー！ねー！ねー！ねー！」
"Right?! Right?!"

1179
01:11:41,112 --> 01:11:43,112
「阿吽の呼吸ができるようになってきた気がする！」
"I feel like we've started getting into breath synchronization!"

1180
01:11:43,112 --> 01:11:45,112
「ね！マジすげえ！」
"Right! Seriously awesome!"

1181
01:11:45,112 --> 01:11:47,112
「私達…よかったー！」
"Us... thank goodness!"

1182
01:11:47,112 --> 01:11:48,612
「通じ合ってるかも！」
"Maybe we're on the same wavelength!"

1183
01:11:48,612 --> 01:11:50,312
「マジ通じ合ってる！しかも50%系当ててけたの強いよね、結構」
"We're seriously on the same wavelength! Plus, landing those 50% choices was pretty clutch."

1184
01:11:50,312 --> 01:11:52,112
「ねー！たしかに！」
"Right! Definitely!"

1185
01:11:52,112 --> 01:11:54,112
「そう、2択大体当たってるから」
"Yeah, we mostly got the 2-way choices right."

1186
01:11:54,112 --> 01:11:56,112
「うん、うん、うん」
"Yeah, yeah, yeah."

1187
01:11:56,112 --> 01:11:58,312
「凄かったー。いやー、なんかもうさ…」
"That was awesome. Man, I really thought..."

1188
01:11:58,312 --> 01:12:00,612
「あのコーヒーあたりどうなることかと思った…」
"I wondered what would happen around that coffee question..."

1189
01:12:00,612 --> 01:12:02,112
「終わったかと思った」
"I thought we were done for!"

1190
01:12:02,112 --> 01:12:04,112
「5時間かかると思って…」
"I thought it would take 5 hours..."

1191
01:12:04,112 --> 01:12:07,612
「コーヒーね、缶コーヒーね。缶コーヒー…」
"Coffee, canned coffee, right. Canned coffee..."

1192
01:12:07,612 --> 01:12:11,112
「いや、でもあの時よりかは、結構正答率上がってたんじゃない？」
"No, but compared to that time, our correct answer rate went up quite a bit, didn't it?"

1193
01:12:11,112 --> 01:12:13,612
「あとさ、みんな忘れちゃいけないの、シンデレラね！」
"Also, everyone shouldn't forget: Cinderella!"

1194
01:12:13,612 --> 01:12:15,612
「そうだった、シンデレラもあった！」
"That's right, Cinderella was there too!"

1195
01:12:15,612 --> 01:12:18,112
「シンデレラね。日本の有名な城？」
"Cinderella, right. 'Famous Japanese castle'?"

1196
01:12:18,112 --> 01:12:20,112
「シンデレラ城！シンデレラ！」
"Cinderella Castle! Cinderella!"

1197
01:12:20,112 --> 01:12:22,112
「違う！」「なんで世界で…」
"No!" / "Why in the world..."

1198
01:12:22,112 --> 01:12:25,612
「世界で…世界で今日なんか有名なやつかと思って…」
"I thought it was a famous one in the world... in the world today..."

1199
01:12:25,612 --> 01:12:28,112
「いや、間違えてないよそれ。一番有名なのはシンデレラ城だと思うけどね」
"No, that wasn't wrong. I do think Cinderella Castle is the most famous, though."

1200
01:12:28,112 --> 01:12:31,112
「まあまあまあ」「でもあれチェーン店じゃからな、言ってみれば」
"Well, well, well." / "Though that's a chain store, if you think about it."

1201
01:12:31,112 --> 01:12:34,112
「チェーン店！？」「言うな！」
"A chain store?!" / "Don't say that!"

1202
01:12:34,112 --> 01:12:38,112
「固有名称じゃなくて…日本支店にあるやつじゃからな、あのシンデレラ」
"Instead of a proper noun... because that Cinderella is just one in the Japan branch."

1203
01:12:38,112 --> 01:12:40,612
「日本に『も』あるね」
"There's one in Japan 'too'!"

1204
01:12:40,612 --> 01:12:43,112
「日本特有のって書いてないよね？」
"It didn't say 'unique to Japan', right?"

1205
01:12:43,112 --> 01:12:45,112
「そうそうそう！」「いやーよかったね、あれは」
"Exactly, exactly!" / "Man, that was great."

1206
01:12:45,112 --> 01:12:46,612
「どうですか？つづり的に…」
"So, how about it? From Tsuzuri's perspective..."

1207
01:12:46,612 --> 01:12:49,112
「自分はお姉さんになれたと思う？今回の『終われまテン』で」
"Do you think you managed to be an 'older sister' in this 'Owarema-ten'?"

1208
01:12:49,112 --> 01:12:51,112
「いやー、まあいつも通りお姉さんだったかなとは…」
"Well, I think I was an older sister as usual..."

1209
01:12:51,112 --> 01:12:53,112
「勿論思ってます、勿論！」
"Of course I think so, of course!"

1210
01:12:53,112 --> 01:12:56,112
「今日のお姉さんポイント、どこがよかった？」
"Which part was your good 'older sister point' today?"

1211
01:12:56,112 --> 01:12:59,112
「いやー、しっかり決めるときは決めたのがね、お姉さんだったかな」
"Well, when it came to sealing the deal, I stepped up—that was very older-sister-like!"

1212
01:12:59,112 --> 01:13:00,112
「あ！でもそれで言うと結構みんな決めてたと思う」
"Ah! But speaking of that, I think everyone stepped up."

1213
01:13:00,112 --> 01:13:03,112
「そぴあも決めてるんだよなー」
"Sopia stepped up too, you know."

1214
01:13:03,112 --> 01:13:05,112
「まあ…たまにはね…」
"Well... once in a while..."

1215
01:13:05,112 --> 01:13:07,612
「たまにがお姉さんか？」
"Only 'once in a while' is older-sister-like?"

1216
01:13:07,612 --> 01:13:10,112
「たまには譲ってあげてもいいんじゃないかなって、お姉さんだから」
"I thought it's fine to yield to others once in a while, because I'm the older sister."

1217
01:13:10,112 --> 01:13:12,612
「おー、上から！」
"Ooh, looking down from above!"

1218
01:13:12,612 --> 01:13:13,612
「はい！」
"Yes!"

1219
01:13:13,612 --> 01:13:15,112
「どうだった？そぴあは」
"How was Sopia?"

1220
01:13:15,112 --> 01:13:17,612
「これそぴあがね、かなりお姉さん常識人なところを…」
"Sopia really showed everyone her mature, sensible older-sister side..."

1221
01:13:17,612 --> 01:13:20,112
「見せられたんじゃないでしょうか！」
"Wouldn't you say she demonstrated that?"

1222
01:13:20,112 --> 01:13:22,112
「確かにそぴあ、結構常識的だったな」
"Indeed, Sopia was quite sensible."

1223
01:13:22,112 --> 01:13:24,612
「変なの、そんなのなかったか」
"Did she have any weird answers?"

1224
01:13:24,612 --> 01:13:26,612
「今回はね！『今回は』なかったね！」
"Not this time! 'This time' she didn't!"

1225
01:13:26,612 --> 01:13:28,612
「私たぶん忘れちゃったんだけど、前回何があったんだっけ？そぴあ」
"I probably forgot, but what did Sopia do last time?"

1226
01:13:28,612 --> 01:13:31,112
「えっとね『ハサミを使う職業といえば？』」
"Well, 'Speaking of an occupation that uses scissors?'"

1227
01:13:31,112 --> 01:13:34,112
「ちょっとコメント欄でも考えてみよう。『ハサミを使う職業といえば』何だと思う？みんな」
"Let's think about it in the chat too. 'Speaking of an occupation that uses scissors', what do you guys think?"

1228
01:13:34,112 --> 01:13:35,612
「ハサミを使う職業…」
"An occupation that uses scissors..."

1229
01:13:35,612 --> 01:13:38,112
「ハサミと言えば…」
"Speaking of scissors..."

1230
01:13:38,112 --> 01:13:40,112
「メインで使う職業と言えばあれですよね」
"Speaking of an occupation where it's used as the main tool, it's that, right?"

1231
01:13:40,112 --> 01:13:42,112
「じゃあ『せーの』でその時の回答言って！その時の回答」
"Then let's say the answer from back then on 'Ready, set'! The answer back then!"

1232
01:13:42,112 --> 01:13:44,612
「え、私なんて言ってたっけ？」
"Wait, what did I say back then?"

1233
01:13:44,612 --> 01:13:46,112
「行くよ？せーの！」
"Here we go! Ready, set!"

1234
01:13:46,112 --> 01:13:48,112
「美容師！」
"Beautician!"

1235
01:13:48,112 --> 01:13:50,112
「ちょっと長いのおったな、何だ？」
"There was someone with a long answer, what was that?"

1236
01:13:50,112 --> 01:13:52,612
「口折れたやついたな、誰だ？」
"Someone's voice faltered, who was it?"

1237
01:13:52,612 --> 01:13:55,112
「つづりは『お花屋さん』って言ったんだよね？」
"Tsuzuri said 'Florist', right?"

1238
01:13:55,112 --> 01:13:57,112
「うん、お花屋さん」
"Yeah, florist."

1239
01:13:57,112 --> 01:13:59,112
「分かるよ、ハサミ使うよね、お花チョキチョキするよね」
"I get it, they use scissors, snip-snapping flowers."

1240
01:13:59,112 --> 01:14:01,112
「で…そぴあさん？」
"And... Sopia-san?"

1241
01:14:01,112 --> 01:14:03,112
「『紙切り師』！」
"'Kamikiri-shi' (paper cutting artist)!"

1242
01:14:03,112 --> 01:14:04,612
「『紙切り師』！？」
"'Paper cutting artist'?!"

1243
01:14:04,612 --> 01:14:06,612
「渋い！」
"So niche!"

1244
01:14:06,612 --> 01:14:08,612
「ほら、ハサミで紙切って凄い絵にする人いるじゃん！」
"Look, there are people who cut paper with scissors to make amazing art, right?!"

1245
01:14:08,612 --> 01:14:10,612
「いるいる！凄いよねアレ！芸術だよね！」
"There are! Those are amazing! It's art!"

1246
01:14:10,612 --> 01:14:13,112
「で、美容師さんとかお花屋さんとかハサミ以外の物も使うけど…」
"And beauticians or florists use other things besides scissors, but..."

1247
01:14:13,112 --> 01:14:16,612
「紙切り師はハサミ1本で…！」
"Paper cutting artists do it with just a single pair of scissors...!"

1248
01:14:16,612 --> 01:14:18,612
「ハサミ1本で勝負してるからね！」
"Because they rely solely on that one pair of scissors!"

1249
01:14:18,612 --> 01:14:21,112
「あー！ハサミ1本で！」
"Ah! With just a single pair of scissors!"

1250
01:14:21,112 --> 01:14:24,112
「そう！」
"Exactly!"

1251
01:14:24,112 --> 01:14:28,112
「ハサミだけしか使わない職業って言えば紙切り師なの！」
"If you talk about an occupation that uses ONLY scissors, it's paper cutting artists!"

1252
01:14:28,112 --> 01:14:32,112
「あー！理屈としては正しい！」「理屈としてはね」
"Ah! The logic is sound!" / "Logically speaking, anyway."

1253
01:14:32,112 --> 01:14:36,112
「一番ハサミ使ってるの誰って言ったら紙切り師なの！」
"If you ask who uses scissors the most, it's paper cutting artists!"

1254
01:14:36,112 --> 01:14:40,112
「確かに…」「ハサミ愛が凄かったんだね」
"True..." / "Her love for scissors was intense."

1255
01:14:40,112 --> 01:14:44,112
「そうそう！」「でもハサミを使う職業といえば…美容師じゃん？普通」
"Yeah yeah!" / "But speaking of an occupation that uses scissors... usually it's beautician, right?"

1256
01:14:44,112 --> 01:14:48,112
「まあねー」
"Well, yeah."

1257
01:14:48,112 --> 01:14:52,112
「今回は不発だったからの、奇天烈解答」
"Her eccentric answers didn't trigger this time, though!"

1258
01:14:52,112 --> 01:14:56,112
「ね！今回は普通に常識人だった！」
"Right! This time she was totally sensible!"

1259
01:14:56,112 --> 01:15:00,112
「ふふっ、お姉さんだからね！」
"Heh heh, because I'm the older sister!"

1260
01:15:00,120 --> 01:15:01,360
1分で…？
In one minute...?

1261
01:15:01,360 --> 01:15:02,280
確かにね。
That's true.

1262
01:15:02,280 --> 01:15:05,800
素晴らしいよね、アートな。すごいよね、本当な。
It's wonderful, art-wise. It's really amazing.

1263
01:15:03,320 --> 01:15:05,800
すごい仕事だよね。
It's an amazing job, isn't it?

1264
01:15:05,800 --> 01:15:09,720
素晴らしい芸術じゃとわしも思うんじゃが…
I also think it's a wonderful art form, but...

1265
01:15:08,620 --> 01:15:10,120
うん、すごいと思う。
Yeah, I think it's amazing.

1266
01:15:09,720 --> 01:15:14,720
ハサミを使う職業と言えばで、あの、アンケートを取ったときに…
When taking a survey on professions that use scissors...

1267
01:15:14,720 --> 01:15:19,560
合わせる気はないよね？
You have no intention of matching, do you?

1268
01:15:18,520 --> 01:15:20,620
いや、そう、職人さんだからね、やっぱりね。
Well, yeah, because they're artisans after all.

1269
01:15:19,560 --> 01:15:27,840
そう、職人さんというのはね、なかなか、あの、母数はそんな多くないイメージがあるけど…
Right, artisans don't really seem to have a large population size, but...

1270
01:15:27,840 --> 01:15:32,520
あ、それとあと、これ、あの、切り絵師っていうらしい。
Ah, and also, apparently it's called paper-cutting artist.

1271
01:15:32,520 --> 01:15:36,560
髪切り師… 髪切り師どっちにしろってことか！
Paper-cutter... Paper-cutter, you mean whichever one!

1272
01:15:36,560 --> 01:15:40,620
切り絵師さん、ごめんなさい！
Paper-cutting artists, I'm sorry!

1273
01:15:40,620 --> 01:15:44,320
なるほどね。切り絵師さんね。
I see. Paper-cutting artists, right?

1274
01:15:44,320 --> 01:15:48,920
光輝と変わんないね、これね、そしたら。光輝と変わんないね。
That's no different from Koki then. No different from Koki.

1275
01:15:48,920 --> 01:15:54,800
ちょっと待って！今なんか2個出されたって何？評価？評価？
Wait a second! What do you mean by two results shown just now? Evaluation? Evaluation?

1276
01:15:52,620 --> 01:15:55,620
変わんないね、そしたらね。同じだね。
It doesn't change then. It's the same.

1277
01:15:54,800 --> 01:16:02,160
キョーコも別にそんなデカいのは、お酒以外はなかったかな？
Kyoko also didn't have anything that huge, except for alcohol, right?

1278
01:16:02,160 --> 01:16:10,960
焼酎の酒って言ったら、一番最初「大五郎」出るからな、マジでな。これ聞いてみ？歌舞伎町で聞いてみたやってみ？マジで。
When you talk about shochu, "Daigoro" comes out first, seriously. Try asking people! Try doing a survey in Kabukicho! Seriously.

1279
01:16:10,960 --> 01:16:21,960
新橋と歌舞伎町で聞いてみたのアンケートでやってみ？そしたら多分「大五郎」って言うから、みんな。
Try running a survey in Shinbashi and Kabukicho! Then everyone will probably say "Daigoro".

1280
01:16:15,920 --> 01:16:21,960
サラリーマンの人は…みんなそれなんだ。「大五郎」なんだ。なるほどね。へー。
Salarymen... are all about that. It's Daigoro. I see. Huh.

1281
01:16:21,960 --> 01:16:29,520
みんな出来上がってるときに聞いてんの、それちなみに。ベロンベロンになってから聞いてる。
By the way, they ask people when they're already wasted. They ask after they're totally plastered.

1282
01:16:25,620 --> 01:16:27,920
しらふのときじゃないんだ。
So not when they're sober.

1283
01:16:29,520 --> 01:16:36,560
え、じゃあキョーコとお酒を飲みに行くってなったら、もしかしたら「大五郎」って出てくる可能性があるってこと？
Eh, so if we go out drinking with Kyoko, is there a chance "Daigoro" might come out?

1284
01:16:36,560 --> 01:16:40,120
お店では出てこないかな、あんまり「大五郎」は。
It doesn't really come out in bars/restaurants, Daigoro.

1285
01:16:39,620 --> 01:16:42,320
どこで飲むお酒なの？家？
Where do you drink that? At home?

1286
01:16:40,920 --> 01:16:42,320
家。
At home.

1287
01:16:42,320 --> 01:16:45,620
え、それめっちゃデッカい奴？
Wait, is it that super huge one?

1288
01:16:45,620 --> 01:16:47,120
4リットルの奴。
The 4-liter one.

1289
01:16:47,120 --> 01:16:50,160
4リットル！？どれくらいで飲むの？一瞬で飲むの？
4 liters!? How fast do you drink it? Do you chug it in an instant?

1290
01:16:50,160 --> 01:16:55,620
いや、一瞬では流石に飲まないね。割るからさ、大体さ。
No, I obviously don't drink it in an instant. I usually dilute it.

1291
01:16:54,920 --> 01:16:57,120
あー、なるほどね。
Ah, I see.

1292
01:16:58,320 --> 01:17:01,120
ガチの酒飲みだな、これは。
She's a real hard drinker, this one.

1293
01:17:00,620 --> 01:17:07,240
お店の焼酎って言ったら、金宮だよね。みんなね。出てくるのね。
When talking about shochu at bars, it's Kinmiya, right? Everyone says Kinmiya.

1294
01:17:07,240 --> 01:17:14,400
コメント欄に共感求めてる。どうなんじゃろ？わしのコメント欄そんなお酒飲みいるかな？
She's seeking empathy from the comments section. I wonder... Are there really that many heavy drinkers in my comment section?

1295
01:17:12,620 --> 01:17:14,400
大体金宮じゃない？
Isn't it usually Kinmiya?

1296
01:17:14,400 --> 01:17:20,520
「おっさんないよ」って言われてる。キョーコおっさんチョイスなの？それもしかして。
They're saying "No way, old man". Is that an old man choice, Kyoko? Could it be?

1297
01:17:18,120 --> 01:17:20,520
大体そうだよね。
Usually, yeah.

1298
01:17:20,520 --> 01:17:26,440
へー。でも確かにキョーコって結構お酒強いみたいな、お話ししてるもんね、確かに。
Hmm. But indeed, Kyoko, you often talk about being quite strong with alcohol.

1299
01:17:26,440 --> 01:17:34,800
うん、でも仕事のために半年断ってるからね、私。頑張ってます、はい。
Yeah, but I've abstained for half a year for work, you know. I'm trying my best, yes.

1300
01:17:30,920 --> 01:17:33,620
えー！すごい！
Wha-! That's amazing!

1301
01:17:34,800 --> 01:17:40,520
やっぱりね、粘膜に悪いから、お酒っていうのは。腫れちゃったりするから。
Well, alcohol is bad for the mucous membranes. It can get swollen.

1302
01:17:38,320 --> 01:17:40,120
喉にね。
For your throat, right?

1303
01:17:40,520 --> 01:17:49,120
ちょっと位なら大丈夫だけど、なんか悪いって分かっていることは、大体避けようと思ってて。
A little bit is fine, but I try to avoid things that I know are bad for me.

1304
01:17:48,920 --> 01:17:50,620
あー、なるほどね。
Ah, I see.

1305
01:17:49,120 --> 01:17:59,920
あえてやりに行く必要ないなって思ってて。
I feel there's no need to go out of my way to do it.

1306
01:17:53,120 --> 01:17:58,120
素晴らしいのじゃ。飲む時は配信とかで飲めばいいですかね、我々達。
That's wonderful. When drinking, maybe we should just drink during streams?

1307
01:17:57,120 --> 01:18:00,120
そうそうそう。プライベートで飲むことはないね、もうね。
Exactly. I don't drink in private anymore.

1308
01:17:59,920 --> 01:18:06,120
なるほどね。え、面白かったなー。
I see. Man, that was fun.

1309
01:18:04,620 --> 01:18:06,120
ね、楽しかった。
Yeah, it was fun.

1310
01:18:05,620 --> 01:18:07,620
みらーはどうだったの？
How was it for Miror?

1311
01:18:06,120 --> 01:18:15,920
みらーはね、あの、人間たちの衝撃的な回答にね、恐れおののいて…
Miror was, well, trembling in fear at humans' shocking answers...

1312
01:18:15,920 --> 01:18:22,520
え、何が一番おののいた？
Eh, what scared you the most?

1313
01:18:18,120 --> 01:18:22,520
コーヒー。コーヒー。
Coffee. Coffee.

1314
01:18:22,520 --> 01:18:27,560
なんか正直、シンデレラジオはコメラに予想してた人いたんだよね。
Honestly, someone in the comment section had already predicted Cinderella Radio.

1315
01:18:27,560 --> 01:18:34,120
え！？いたの！？すごい！「誰かシンデレラジオって答えるだろ」みたいに言ってた人がいて。
What!? There was!? That's amazing! Someone said, "Surely someone will answer Cinderella Radio."

1316
01:18:34,120 --> 01:18:39,720
理解手じゃん！まさか居ないだろと思ってたけど…
They get it! Though I thought no way anyone would actually say it...

1317
01:18:37,120 --> 01:18:39,720
すっげーな！
That's awesome!

1318
01:18:39,720 --> 01:18:47,920
そう。でも多分、コメント欄を以てしても、コーヒーは想像つかないと…
Yeah. But even with the comments section combined, coffee is unimaginable...

1319
01:18:44,620 --> 01:18:47,920
コーヒーは凄すぎる！
Coffee is just too absurd!

1320
01:18:47,920 --> 01:18:52,120
図書企画じゃあないよ！
It's not a library project!

1321
01:18:52,120 --> 01:18:59,920
いやいや、でもだって3文字に収めるってなったらさ… あの、削るとしたら「あと」かなって思って…
No no, but if you have to fit it into 3 letters... I thought if I were to trim it, maybe "ato"...

1322
01:18:59,920 --> 01:19:05,400
なんで削るんだよ、そもそも！3文字に収めてくださいじゃないのよ、そう。
Why trim it in the first place?! It wasn't "Please fit it into 3 letters"!

1323
01:19:05,400 --> 01:19:10,120
そうでした。ごめんなさい、次もしあったら… 「コーヒー」で書きますよ、もう！
That's true. I'm sorry, if there's a next time... I'll write "Coffee" then!

1324
01:19:10,120 --> 01:19:18,120
3文字で戦ってほしいな、できれば。最初から3文字で生まれた子を連れてきてほしい、最初から。
I want you to fight with 3 letters if possible! Bring a word born with 3 letters from the start!

1325
01:19:18,120 --> 01:19:26,520
確かに！わかりました。次はちゃんと3文字持ってきます！
Indeed! Understood. Next time I'll bring proper 3 letters!

1326
01:19:25,120 --> 01:19:27,120
はい、お願いします！
Yes, please!

1327
01:19:26,520 --> 01:19:35,920
またやりたいよね。まだまだいろんなニーズがあるんだよ。「おわれまテン1」と「2」とかあって、今回「1」で遊んだんじゃけど、違うのでも…
I'd like to do this again. There are still various options. There's 'Owarema-ten 1' and '2', and we played '1' this time, but with different...

1328
01:19:35,920 --> 01:19:39,120
2しよ！2したいよね！
Let's do 2! We want to play 2!

1329
01:19:39,120 --> 01:19:45,720
わしたちさ、したいコラボが多すぎてさ、間に合ってなくない？正直。
We have too many collabs we want to do, aren't we running out of time? Honestly.

1330
01:19:45,720 --> 01:19:59,920
そうなんだよ。4人コラボもさ、後で報告しますのでお持ちくださいね、人間たち。そーぴーとさ、わし、まだつづりとコラボできてないんだよね。
Yeah. And for our 4-person collab, we'll announce it later so please wait, humans. Sopy and I haven't done a 1-on-1 collab with Tsuzuri yet, you know.

1331
01:19:55,120 --> 01:19:59,920
そっか！1対1のコラボしようって予定を結構デビュー直後くらいに立ててたんじゃけど…
Right! We made plans for 1-on-1 collabs right after debut, but...

1332
01:20:00,128 --> 01:20:03,278
やるつもりだったゲームが実はまだリリースされてなかったっぽくて...
The game we were planning to play actually hadn't been released yet...

1333
01:20:03,278 --> 01:20:05,728
そうなんだよ！ うん。
That's right! Yeah.

1334
01:20:05,928 --> 01:20:11,928
で、なんか待ってても、多分まだっぽいから、じゃあ違うのをやってみよう！
So even if we wait, it probably won't come out for a while, so let's try playing something else!

1335
01:20:12,128 --> 01:20:14,328
ね、違うゲームやってみたいよね。
Yeah, we want to try playing different games, right?

1336
01:20:14,328 --> 01:20:16,628
お！ やりたい！
Oh! We want to!

1337
01:20:16,628 --> 01:20:21,628
そう、だからゲーム考えて、ちょっと今からスケジュール決めるから、もし先になっちゃうかもじゃけど、やりたいよね。
So we'll think of games and set the schedule, and even if it's further down the road, we want to do it, right?

1338
01:20:21,628 --> 01:20:25,328
うん、やりたい！ 勝ちたい！
Yeah, I want to! I want to win!

1339
01:20:25,328 --> 01:20:27,328
あ、協力ゲームかもしれないし...
Ah, it might be a co-op game...

1340
01:20:27,328 --> 01:20:29,928
勝ちたいって言った時点で協力ゲームなくなった！
The moment you said "I want to win," it stopped being a co-op game!

1341
01:20:29,928 --> 01:20:33,128
勝ちたい！ 他殺確定した！
I want to win! PvP confirmed!

1342
01:20:33,328 --> 01:20:37,128
やっぱりなんか、蹴落とし合いたいんよね。 なかなかね！
After all, we want to knock each other down, don't we? Exactly!

1343
01:20:37,128 --> 01:20:41,628
ゲームと言えばになっちゃってるよね、戦うものっていう。 ゲームと言えば相手をね、ヘッドショット！
We've been assuming games mean fighting each other. When you think of games, it's about headshotting your opponent!

1344
01:20:44,128 --> 01:20:49,128
いやいや、でも協力ゲームも確かにやってみたさあるな... いやでも、なんかいろんなゲームやりたくて本当迷っちゃうよね。
No, but I definitely want to try co-op games too... But honestly, there are so many games I want to play, I really can't decide.

1345
01:20:49,128 --> 01:20:51,628
ね、4人でやりたいゲームいっぱいあるよね。
Yeah, there are so many games we want to play together as four, right?

1346
01:20:51,628 --> 01:20:54,128
ある！ あのね、リスト作ったんだよね、うちらね。
There are! You know, we actually made a list.

1347
01:20:54,128 --> 01:20:56,328
そう、作った作った！ デビュー前にね！
Yeah, we made one! Before our debut!

1348
01:20:56,328 --> 01:20:58,328
そう！ で、1個もできてないよね？
Right! And we haven't done a single one yet, right?

1349
01:20:58,328 --> 01:21:04,628
確かに！ マジで1個もできてないの！ 確かに！
Indeed! Seriously, not a single one! Exactly!

1350
01:21:04,628 --> 01:21:08,928
そうなんだよね。なんか、時間が足りてないんじゃよね、わしたち。
That's right. It feels like we just don't have enough time.

1351
01:21:09,128 --> 01:21:10,928
ねぇ〜
I know~

1352
01:21:10,928 --> 01:21:13,928
今開いたんだけどさ、ちょっと言っていい？ いいよ！
I just opened it now, can I read them out? Go ahead!

1353
01:21:14,328 --> 01:21:19,628
えー、『Overcooked!』『Unrailed!』『R.E.P.O.』やって、1個目は終わった、できた。で『Move or Die』...
Um, "Overcooked!," "Unrailed!," "R.E.P.O."—wait, the first one is done. Then "Move or Die"...

1354
01:21:19,628 --> 01:21:25,628
『マリオパーティ』『DAVE THE DIVER』『ワードウルフ』『桃鉄』『めっちゃカメレオン』『Chained Together』
"Mario Party," "DAVE THE DIVER," "Wordwolf," "Momotetsu," "Super Chameleon," "Chained Together"...

1355
01:21:25,628 --> 01:21:31,628
『Human: Fall Flat』『Party Animals』『Big Walk』『Overboss』『Lethal Company』
"Human: Fall Flat," "Party Animals," "Big Walk," "Overboss," "Lethal Company"...

1356
01:21:31,628 --> 01:21:36,128
『みんなでチキン度診断』『リズム天国』『ito』
"Chicken Meter," "Rhythm Heaven," "ito"...

1357
01:21:36,128 --> 01:21:41,628
『たった今考えたプロポーズの言葉を君に捧ぐよ。』『ヘルパゴス』『GANG BEASTS』...
"I'll Give You the Proposal Words I Just Came Up With," "Hellapagos," "Gang Beasts"...

1358
01:21:41,628 --> 01:21:45,128
みたいな感じでおっぱいあるんじゃよ！
There are tons like that!

1359
01:21:45,128 --> 01:21:50,128
読み切れないぐらいっぱいあるのにもかかわらず... そうそうそう！
Even though there are so many we can't even read them all... Right right right!

1360
01:21:50,128 --> 01:21:54,128
全然できてないから、ちょっとずつやっていきたいよね、わしたちでね。
We haven't done them at all, so we want to play them little by little together, right?

1361
01:21:54,128 --> 01:21:58,628
ねー！ 今スクロール、今3回下行った、ちなみに。で、それで最後に行った。
Yeah! I scrolled down three times just now, by the way, and that's how I got to the end.

1362
01:21:58,628 --> 01:22:04,628
そうなんじゃよね。で、せっかくだし、わしたち4人で次やるコラボの話言っちゃう？
That's true. And since we're at it, should we talk about our next 4-player collab?

1363
01:22:04,628 --> 01:22:07,628
おー！ 言っちゃう！
Ooh! Let's say it!

1364
01:22:07,628 --> 01:22:13,628
わしたち、初めての先輩コラボの日にホロ鯖マイクラをやったよね。
On the day of our very first collab with seniors, we played Minecraft on the Hololive server, right?

1365
01:22:13,628 --> 01:22:15,628
やったー！ 楽しかった！
We did! That was fun!

1366
01:22:15,628 --> 01:22:22,128
楽しかったよね。でもあれってさ、マイクラの観光をしたけど、マイクラのゲームとして...
It was fun, right? But that was touring Minecraft; as an actual Minecraft game...

1367
01:22:22,128 --> 01:22:27,628
こう、なんじゃろな、建築したりとか、敵を倒したりとか、そういうのはあんまりしてないよね。
like building things or defeating enemies, we haven't really done much of that, right?

1368
01:22:27,628 --> 01:22:29,928
できてないね。
We haven't.

1369
01:22:29,928 --> 01:22:34,128
ということで、しかもキョーコってマイクラ1回もしたことないんだよね、確か。
And on top of that, Kyoko has never played Minecraft even once before, right?

1370
01:22:34,128 --> 01:22:37,628
ないのよ！ そうなの！ ゲーマーなのにもかかわらず！
Never! That's right! Even though I'm a gamer!

1371
01:22:37,628 --> 01:22:40,128
そうそう、逆張りだから私！
Yeah, yeah, because I'm a contrarian!

1372
01:22:40,128 --> 01:22:47,628
つづりもあんまりないの？ あんまりないね。なんか、ちょこっと触ってみたことはあるけれど、全然わかんない。
Tsuzuri hasn't played much either? Not really. I touched it just a tiny bit, but I have no idea how to play.

1373
01:22:47,628 --> 01:22:53,128
ということで、アソビ★まわり隊4人でマイクラをしませんか！
So, why don't the four of us in Asobi Mawaritai play Minecraft?!

1374
01:22:53,128 --> 01:22:57,128
やりたいーー！
We want to--!!

1375
01:22:57,128 --> 01:23:04,128
そう、あのマイクラね、配信でやってみたいなって思ってたから、4人でやろうって話をしていて...
Yeah, I really wanted to try playing Minecraft on stream, so we've been discussing doing it together...

1376
01:23:04,128 --> 01:23:07,928
えっとね、11月の21日、来週かな？
Umm, November 21st, next week maybe?

1377
01:23:07,928 --> 01:23:10,628
21日！ そうだね、来週だ！
The 21st! Yeah, that's next week!

1378
01:23:10,628 --> 01:23:15,128
来週の土曜日の、今のところ、お昼の13時から...
Next Saturday, as of now, starting from 1:00 PM...

1379
01:23:15,128 --> 01:23:20,928
午後1時から遊ぶ予定なんだよね。
We're planning to play starting at 1:00 PM.

1380
01:23:20,928 --> 01:23:26,628
ちょっとあの、お仕事のスケジュール的に絶対に確定とは言えないんじゃけど...
Because of work schedules, we can't say it's 100% set in stone, but...

1381
01:23:26,628 --> 01:23:33,128
今、4人でマイクラしたいねってお話をしているので、ぜひお見知りおきを...見に来てほしいのじゃ！
right now we're talking about wanting to play Minecraft as four, so please keep an eye out and come watch!

1382
01:23:33,128 --> 01:23:36,128
やったー！
Yay!

1383
01:23:36,128 --> 01:23:39,128
他になんかお知らせとかある人いる？
Does anyone else have any announcements?

1384
01:23:39,128 --> 01:23:43,928
いなそう？ 今のところ大丈夫そう？
No one? Everything good for now?

1385
01:23:43,928 --> 01:23:47,128
1個だけ、みんなに頼んでいいかな？ はーい！
Can I ask everyone just one favor? Sure!

1386
01:23:47,128 --> 01:23:51,628
私、明日ラオーラ先輩のお家にお呼ばれされていて...
Tomorrow, I've been invited to Raora-senpai's house...

1387
01:23:51,628 --> 01:23:57,128
お家... 私の無事を祈っていてくれると嬉しいです、みんなで。
Her house... I'd be really happy if everyone prayed for my safety.

1388
01:23:57,128 --> 01:24:01,928
え？ なになになに？ なんでそういうテンションなん？ なんかあったん？
Eh? What what what? Why are you sounding like that? Did something happen?

1389
01:24:01,928 --> 01:24:06,128
あのね、ラオーラ先輩ってイタリアの方でしょ？
Well, Raora-senpai is Italian, right?

1390
01:24:06,128 --> 01:24:11,628
で、なんか日本料理を教えてほしいって言われたから...「じゃあナポリタンはどうですか？」って言ったの。
And she asked me to teach her Japanese cooking... so I said, "How about Neapolitan?"

1391
01:24:11,628 --> 01:24:15,628
終わったー！！ なんでイタリア人にナポリタン？！
You're doomed!! Why Neapolitan to an Italian?!

1392
01:24:15,628 --> 01:24:18,628
なんでよ！ 他にいっぱい選択肢あるだろ！ 日本料理にしておけよ！
Why?! There are so many other options! Stick to Japanese food!

1393
01:24:18,628 --> 01:24:22,128
違うんだよ！ あのね、オムライスって先に言われたの。
No, listen! She said omurice first.

1394
01:24:22,128 --> 01:24:26,128
あ、じゃあ洋食がいいんだって思って。
Ah, so I thought Yoshoku was good.

1395
01:24:26,128 --> 01:24:32,128
日本料理の中でも多分もう日本に住んでるから、じゃあ一通りの日本食行けるんだなって思って、「じゃあナポリタンはどうですか？」って。
Since she already lives in Japan, I figured she must be used to standard Japanese food, so I asked, "How about Neapolitan?"

1396
01:24:32,128 --> 01:24:35,928
なんでパスタにした？！ ガチでなんでパスタにした？！
Why did you choose pasta?! Seriously, why pasta?!

1397
01:24:35,928 --> 01:24:39,128
ナポリタン... チャレンジャーすぎない、ちょっと？
Neapolitan... Isn't that being a bit too much of a challenger?

1398
01:24:39,128 --> 01:24:43,128
あのね、違うんだよ。私、ナポリタンに超自信あるのよ。
No, listen. I'm super confident in my Neapolitan.

1399
01:24:43,128 --> 01:24:48,628
で、あのケチャップのこと...パスタにケチャップかけるのがタブーってことは知ってるのよ、元々。
And I already know that putting ketchup on pasta is a taboo over there.

1400
01:24:48,628 --> 01:24:54,128
よくInstagramで流れてくるから。パスタに厳しい人たちの動画が。
Because videos of people being strict about pasta show up on my Instagram all the time.

1401
01:24:54,128 --> 01:25:00,136
あれ見て知ってたんだけど、「私のナポリタンだったら落とせる！」って思ったら、そもそもチャンスすら与えられず...
I knew it from watching those, but I thought, "I can win her over with my Neapolitan!", but I wasn't even given a chance...

1402
01:25:02,296 --> 01:25:05,876
え、もう私、地下牢獄が決まってしまったので...
Well, my stay in the underground dungeon has already been decided...

1403
01:25:05,936 --> 01:25:08,656
そんな攻めるんじゃないよ！
Don't be so aggressive!

1404
01:25:09,816 --> 01:25:16,036
あ、行けるかなと思って... なんかここで、もし私のナポリタンで感動してもらえたら、ちょっと文化の扉1個開けんなと思って...
Ah, I thought I could make it work... Like, if I could move people with my Napolitan pasta here, I thought maybe I could open up a new cultural door...

1405
01:25:16,936 --> 01:25:20,136
そんな言葉にすることすら禁忌だった。
Even putting it into words was taboo.

1406
01:25:20,936 --> 01:25:22,636
喧嘩売りにいってるのよ！
You're literally picking a fight!

1407
01:25:22,816 --> 01:25:25,696
そう、言葉にすることすらダメだったから...
Yeah, even putting it into words wasn't allowed...

1408
01:25:27,836 --> 01:25:33,536
それで、来週のマイクラコラボに来れるといいな...
So, I hope you can still make it to next week's Minecraft collab...

1409
01:25:33,936 --> 01:25:36,636
え、多分無理で。ちなみにそれだけじゃなくて私...
Uh, probably impossible. By the way, that's not all...

1410
01:25:36,836 --> 01:25:47,436
昨日ね、ホラーゲームをやったのよ、自分の枠で。で、その枠で、ゲームに言わされちゃったんだけど、「パイナップルピザはイタリアのピザより全然美味しいです」っていうセリフがあったの。
Yesterday, I played a horror game on my channel. And in that stream, the game forced me to read a line that said, "Pineapple pizza is way tastier than Italian pizza."

1411
01:25:47,636 --> 01:25:50,136
なんでそんな文化的な喧嘩を売りにいくん？
Why are you going around picking cultural fights?!

1412
01:25:50,136 --> 01:25:54,136
読んじゃったの、私！読んだあとに、はっ！って...
I read it out loud! And after reading it, I went, "Ah!"...

1413
01:25:54,836 --> 01:25:58,336
大丈夫？わしと一緒に炎上講習とか受ける？
Are you okay? Want to take a PR crisis management course with me?

1414
01:25:58,636 --> 01:26:00,136
切り抜かれちゃったの、それ！
It already got clipped!

1415
01:26:00,186 --> 01:26:03,136
終わった！バレちゃった！
It's over! You got exposed!

1416
01:26:03,336 --> 01:26:08,036
だからもしや今日もなんかすごい攻めた発言を繰り返していた？もうどうなってもいいと思っている？
Is that why you kept making super aggressive comments today too? Do you just not care what happens to you anymore?

1417
01:26:08,136 --> 01:26:11,136
もういいやと思って。明日で終わるから私、と思ってさ！
I was like, "Whatever, my career ends tomorrow anyway!"

1418
01:26:13,936 --> 01:26:17,136
だってピザとさ、パスタ、ダブルで行っちゃったもん、私。
Because I did a double combo with both pizza and pasta!

1419
01:26:17,336 --> 01:26:19,136
もうなら全部言っておく？
Then why not just say everything?

1420
01:26:19,336 --> 01:26:21,136
あ、もう全部言っておく？じゃあ。
Ah, should I just say everything then?

1421
01:26:21,336 --> 01:26:23,136
今なら...
Now's your chance...

1422
01:26:23,136 --> 01:26:24,936
センシティブな絵描かせろ、今！じゃあ！
Let me draw sensitive artwork right now, then!

1423
01:26:25,136 --> 01:26:30,136
やばいやばいやばい！ダメダメダメ！良くない良くない！
No no no, dangerous! Not good!

1424
01:26:30,636 --> 01:26:36,136
まあまあまあみたいなね、結構なかなか危ないコラボがあるみたいなので、どうかご無心を...
Well, well, it seems like we have quite a dangerous collab coming up, so please wish us luck...

1425
01:26:36,336 --> 01:26:40,136
アソビ★まわり隊4人でいさせてくださいの、じゃあ...
Please let all 4 of us stay in Asobi Mawaritai!...

1426
01:26:40,336 --> 01:26:43,136
お願いします... 頑張ってきます！
Please... We'll do our best!

1427
01:26:43,136 --> 01:26:46,136
乞うご期待で！
Stay tuned!

1428
01:26:46,336 --> 01:26:51,636
来週のマイクラみんなで一緒にやりたいから！みんなでできるように...
Because I want us all to play Minecraft together next week! So that we can all do it...

1429
01:26:52,636 --> 01:26:56,636
今後を祈ってて、みんな！私のために祈りを捧げて！
Pray for my future, everyone! Offer your prayers for me!

1430
01:26:57,136 --> 01:26:59,136
高括らずのじゃ！
Don't jump to conclusions, noja!

1431
01:26:59,336 --> 01:27:03,136
はい、ありがとう！ありがとうございました！それでは...
Yes, thank you! Thank you very much! Well then...

1432
01:27:03,336 --> 01:27:07,136
あ、あとショートさ、いっぱい出てるの、みんな見てくれてるかな？
Ah, also, we have lots of Shorts coming out, I wonder if everyone's watching them?

1433
01:27:07,236 --> 01:27:11,936
アソビ★まわり隊公式ショート頑張ってるよね！
The official Asobi Mawaritai Shorts team is working hard!

1434
01:27:12,136 --> 01:27:14,336
毎日上がってるから！そう！
They're uploaded every day! Yeah!

1435
01:27:14,636 --> 01:27:20,136
なので是非是非、アソビ★まわり隊公式のX等もチェックしてもらえればと思います。よろしくお願いします！
So please be sure to check out the official Asobi Mawaritai X account and more. Thank you!

1436
01:27:20,936 --> 01:27:23,136
のじゃ！お願いしまーす！
Noja! Please do!

1437
01:27:23,336 --> 01:27:35,636
あとですね、動画の概要欄に3人のチャンネルURLも貼ってありますので、そちらからアソビ★まわり隊全員のチャンネル登録、そしてこの動画の高評価を押してくれると、とっても嬉しいのじゃ！
And also, the channel URLs of the other 3 members are linked in the video description box, so we'd be super happy if you'd subscribe to all members of Asobi Mawaritai and hit the like button on this video, noja!

1438
01:27:36,136 --> 01:27:39,136
のじゃー！
Noja~!

1439
01:27:39,336 --> 01:27:42,636
そんな感じかな？他は大丈夫そう？
Is that about it? Is everything else good?

1440
01:27:42,736 --> 01:27:46,936
うん、大丈夫。忘れてるの無い？大丈夫そう？
Yep, good. Nothing forgotten? Looks good?

1441
01:27:47,136 --> 01:27:56,936
はい！というわけで、今日のアソビ★まわり隊の配信はおしまいなのじゃ！感想はハッシュタグ #アソビまわり隊 でツイートしてくれると嬉しいのじゃ！
Yes! So, that's all for today's Asobi Mawaritai stream, noja! We'd be happy if you tweet your thoughts with the hashtag #アソビまわり隊!

1442
01:27:57,136 --> 01:27:59,636
お願いしまーす！
Please do!

1443
01:27:59,936 --> 01:28:04,636
じゃあ最後の挨拶は、わしが「次も」って言ったら「アソビ★まわり隊」って言うから...
Then for our final greeting, when I say "Next time too,", you say "Asobi Mawaritai!"...

1444
01:28:04,736 --> 01:28:07,636
最初にもやってなくない？
Didn't we not do that at the beginning either?

1445
01:28:07,736 --> 01:28:14,136
やってないじゃん！あー！誰？お姉さんが、お姉さんがとか言い始めた人！
We didn't do it! Ah! Who was the one who started saying "Big sister, big sister"?!

1446
01:28:14,336 --> 01:28:20,636
それ、流れのせいだからね！めらじゃなかったっけ？あれ、つづりからだっけ？
That was because of the flow of conversation! Wasn't it Mela? Wait, was it Tsuzuri?

1447
01:28:20,736 --> 01:28:24,136
先に... めらっちか！
First... was it Melatchi?!

1448
01:28:24,236 --> 01:28:31,136
めらが言ったのは、配信に乗る前に、なんか言ってたからじゃない？電話の段階で確か誰かが言ってて...
The reason Mela said it was because someone said it before the stream went live, right? During the phone call phase, someone said it...

1449
01:28:32,136 --> 01:28:36,636
あれ？誰だ？言ってたの、ちょっと！お姉さんぶりたいんだからいつも！
Wait, who was it that said it?! You always want to act like the big sister!

1450
01:28:36,736 --> 01:28:42,636
ちょっと記憶が... 記憶が無いな...
My memory... I have no memory of this...

1451
01:28:43,136 --> 01:28:55,136
配信始まる前の電話の段階でつづりとかが言ってたよね？つづりとかがね！ソフィア？ソフィア？
Before the stream started, during the call, Tsuzuri or someone said it, right? Tsuzuri or someone! Sofia? Sofia?

1452
01:28:55,336 --> 01:28:59,936
はい！じゃあもうキリがないのでおしまいにしますのじゃ！
Okay! Well, since this is going nowhere, we're wrapping it up, noja!

1453
01:29:00,036 --> 01:29:08,636
行くよ！次もー！ アソビ★まわり隊ー！バイバーイなのじゃー！
Here we go! Next time too—! Asobi Mawaritai~! Bye-bye, noja~!

1454
01:29:13,136 --> 01:29:52,136
[Text: ご視聴感謝なのじゃ！]
[Text: Thank you for watching, noja!]

